{
  "id": "colony_workers",
  "name": "Colony Workers -> Stockpile",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note",
      "type": "Comment",
      "x": 20,
      "y": -120,
      "params": {
        "text": "The worker/stockpile side of production (spec/systems/colony.md §3). Each AssignWorker puts a colonist on a terrain tile (a raw good, yield read LIVE from @UNFORESTED/@FORESTED/@OTHER by terrain id) or in a building (Hammers/Crosses/Bells). ColonyProduce then runs them all: tile yields pass through the tory/expert adjust, building workers use the base rate, and the result accrues into colony0.stockpile.<good> (capped by the warehouse) plus net food/bells/hammers/crosses. Edit a terrain's yield in the Tables tab and the numbers here change with no code."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "trig",
      "type": "OnColonyProduction",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 60,
      "params": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "farmer",
